From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 17:57:54 +0530
Subject: drm/xe: Add SVM headers and notifier API surface

Provide SVM definitions and notifier-lock macros in headers (e.g.
xe_svm.h, xe_userptr.h) so the driver exposes a stable API surface
for SVM and userptr functionality regardless of upstream GPUSVM
availability. Add inline helpers and safe return semantics used by C
codepaths, and centralized fallback declarations that keep build
boundaries clean when CPTCFG_DRM_XE_GPUSVM is disabled.

Signed-off-by: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_userptr.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_userptr.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_userptr.h
index b8ef11f..47fcbb1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_userptr.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_userptr.h
@@ -104,4 +104,8 @@ static inline void xe_vma_userptr_force_invalidate(struct xe_userptr_vma *uvma)
 {
 }
 #endif
+#if !IS_ENABLED(CPTCFG_DRM_XE_GPUSVM)
+int xe_gup_populate_range(struct xe_userptr_vma *uvma);
+void xe_gup_free_sg(struct xe_userptr_vma *uvma);
+#endif
 #endif
